# Note editors

A note that is saved on its own (day note, morning note, night-food meal note, night-eating reason, what helped, custom-metric note, weekly note, and any new one) uses a single pattern. Do not add a bare input, a bare textarea, or a second row of save/cancel buttons.

1. **Collapsed.** No saved text: a pencil (or the surface’s existing add control, such as weekly’s “Add weekly note”). Do not show an empty saved-note box.
2. **Editing.** `NoteEditRow` — the label with ✓ and × on the title row, and a full-width textarea. ✓ commits trimmed non-blank text and leaves edit mode; it stays disabled while the draft is blank. × discards the draft and restores the last saved text. If nothing was saved, × collapses back to the pencil. Do not commit on each keystroke.
3. **Saved.** `NoteDisplayBlock` — the text, a pencil to edit again, and trash. Trash asks with `ConfirmDeleteEntryBar` before clearing. A weekly note may keep its truncated preview and “show full / show less” control; opening it still uses `NoteEditRow`.
4. **Shared component.** New collapsed notes use `NoteEditor` (`src/features/daily-log/NoteEditor.tsx`), which is this cycle. Callers that already render `NoteEditRow` / `NoteDisplayBlock` with the same save, cancel, and confirmed delete stay on those pieces.

A text field that is only part of a larger form, and is stored when that form’s own Save runs (a dish note, the always-visible note on Breakfast / Lunch / Dinner / Snack), is not a separate note editor. Do not give it a second save control.
